# RimMaster campaign repo — ignore rules
#
# Exclude the entire mod_sources tree. These are ~50 third-party RimWorld mods
# pulled locally for auditing only — licensing + size make them a poor fit for
# the repo. They stay on disk, just untracked. (Moved under mods/ in the
# 2026-08-08 reorg, then to vendor/ by RESTRUCTURE stage 2; the bare-name rule
# matches at any depth, the explicit path is belt-and-suspenders.)
#
# 🔴 139 MB as of 2026-08-20 (was 430 MB; the nine stale Outer-Rim branch trees
# were deleted). If this rule ever stops matching, one `git add` makes the whole
# tree permanent in history — plan §4 dep 7, the exact reason .gitignore is
# edited in the same commit as the move.
#
# ⚠️ Written as /** so the SOURCES.md negation below is reachable. Excluding the
# DIRECTORY (`vendor/mod_sources/`) makes git skip it entirely and no `!` line
# under it can ever re-include anything — the same defect that silently untracked
# observed/genome/scan_manifest.json for five days.
mod_sources/**
vendor/mod_sources/**
!vendor/mod_sources/SOURCES.md

# macOS cruft
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Editor/OS noise
*.swp
*~
Thumbs.db

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# src/Jawa/art_bench/<machine>/ is the image-generation bench, not an archive. The
# pipeline writes _raw (model output) then _cut (chroma-keyed) for every attempt,
# at 2-3 MB each; the smelter bench reached 143 MB in about ninety minutes. The
# finals get copied into the mod's own Textures/ and are tracked there, so these
# two stages are pure scaffolding. Deliberate keeps — style candidates, ladder
# contact sheets — are tracked explicitly and are unaffected by these rules.
src/Jawa/art_bench/*/*_raw.png
src/Jawa/art_bench/*/*_cut.png

# Generated report artifacts (reproducible via the Utils/ tools)
*_preview.png
*_legend.json
*_items.md
*_items.json
*_ideoligions.md
*_ideoligions.json

# hand_authored_maps/: study library of downloaded RimWorld .rws maps (~470MB).
# Keep the README manifest in git; the map payloads live on disk only (GDrive).
# Moved to research/RimMandrake/ by RESTRUCTURE stage 1 — it is material we did
# not author but do summarise. The bare-name rules would still match at any
# depth; the explicit paths are kept so the intent survives a future move.
research/RimMandrake/hand_authored_maps/**/*.rws
research/RimMandrake/hand_authored_maps/**/*.zip
research/RimMandrake/hand_authored_maps/**/*.map
research/RimMandrake/hand_authored_maps/**/*.dll
research/RimMandrake/hand_authored_maps/**/*.exe
research/RimMandrake/hand_authored_maps/**/*.pdb
research/RimMandrake/hand_authored_maps/**/*.cs
research/RimMandrake/hand_authored_maps/**/*.csproj
research/RimMandrake/hand_authored_maps/**/*.config
research/RimMandrake/hand_authored_maps/SickBoyWi_RimWorldMaps/

# C# / .NET build intermediates (mods/dev/*). The mod DLL itself IS tracked —
# it is the deliverable and the game needs it — but MSBuild's obj/ tree is
# regenerable noise and churns on every build.
obj/
**/obj/
*.user

# The RimBridge COMPANION build output. Unlike the mod DLLs above, this one is
# NOT a deliverable: bridgetools/build.py rebuilds it unconditionally before
# every deploy (main() calls build() first, and build() exits on a missing SDK),
# so the committed copy was never the thing that shipped. It also embeds the git
# HEAD SHA, so it churned on every commit by any agent with no source change.
# Provenance moved to the deployed DLL's own stamp, which describes the GAME copy
# rather than the repo -- see plan_deploy() and traps.md. Untracked 2026-08-12.
src/RimMandrake/bridgetools/artifacts/

# Per-session agent role records, written by Utils/set_agent_window.sh and read
# by .claude/hooks/set_session_title.py to name the CONVERSATION (the second
# namespace Rule 0 covers). Keyed by Claude Code session id, so every entry is
# machine-local and dies with the session — never shared, never committed.
.claude/session_roles/

# Art review sheets — working images for the owner to eyeball, not
# deliverables. Regenerated freely and often; never part of a mod.
src/Jawa/art_bench/_review/

# Harvested game logs: unreproducible but TRANSIENT — see CLAUDE.md.
# They must survive long enough to be triaged, which disk does. Their value is
# the findings, which go in docs; the raw log is dead weight a week later and
# git keeps every version of it forever. Moved under observed/<stamp>/logs/ by
# the option-B restructure; the observed/**/logs/ rule below covers it, and the
# bare-name rule here is kept so a log dropped anywhere is still refused.
**/logs/Player*.log

# Quarantined payloads: the README is tracked, the corpses are not.
infrastructure/disposing/*/

# observed/<stamp>/ — one directory per live-game contact. TRACK THE MANIFEST,
# NEVER THE PAYLOAD. git never forgets: a save committed once is permanent, and
# untracking it later shrinks nothing. The rule is about refusing the NEXT
# payload. Full statement in observed/README.md.
#
# Saves.
observed/**/*.rws
# Harvested logs — unreproducible but transient; the findings go in a doc.
observed/**/*.log
observed/**/logs/
# 🔴 The SECOND observed root. `observed/**` above only anchors at the repo root,
# so a 148 MB Player.log under infrastructure/state/observed/ was NOT covered —
# found untracked and stageable 2026-08-22. A file that size hard-rejects the
# push for EVERY seat until it is rewritten out of history.
infrastructure/state/observed/**/*.log
infrastructure/state/observed/**/Player.log*
infrastructure/state/observed/**/logs/
# Def dumps — 1.3 GB regenerable; the manifest beside them is the work product.
observed/**/DefDump/
observed/**/defs/
observed/**/Defs/
# Extracted sprite caches, wherever they land — re-extractable from the game's
# own assets. The genome scan's was 351 MB / 14k PNGs; see the genome block below.
observed/**/art_cache/
# Raw validator transcripts — 1.9 MB for one patch run, fully regenerable from the
# command, and the verdict that matters is three lines. The summary .md beside it IS
# the work product and is committed.
observed/preload/*.txt
# Bridge latency probes and screenshots.
observed/**/latency_*.json
observed/**/screenshots/
# Derived save reports (the .rws they came from is not here either).
observed/**/*_preview.png
observed/**/*_legend.json
observed/**/*_items.md
observed/**/*_items.json
observed/**/*_ideoligions.md
observed/**/*_ideoligions.json

# genome scan — bulk cache, regenerated by genome_scan.py + genome_art_cache.py
# from the installed mods. scan_manifest.json IS tracked: it is the provenance
# (counts, game version) for the register the scan produces.
observed/genome/genes.json
observed/genome/xenotypes.json
observed/genome/art_cache/

# mapsynth run outputs — the generator's own artifacts, kept beside it rather
# than in observed/ because they are not game state (plan §3). Everything here
# is reproducible from the .py one level up. The existing run outputs stay
# tracked (untracking them shrinks nothing, git never forgets); this rule
# refuses the NEXT one.
src/RimMandrake/mapsynth/runs/

# ── Large payloads: on disk, never in history ──────────────────────────────
# Added 2026-08-13 with the history re-init. These five files were ~120 MB of a
# 278 MB .git. Git never forgets a committed blob, so the ONLY fix is to not add
# them — see observed/README.md. They stay on disk; they are just untracked.
*.rws
research/**/*.pdf
vendor/salvage/**/*.dll
# Bulk census/dump output and raw load triage: derived, transient, and large.
# One blanket add away from being in history forever (audit #7, 2026-08-13).
design/Jawa/art/census_building_graphics.tsv
observed/quicktest_terrain_top_250x250.json
observed/2026-08-13_load_1730_triage.txt

# Claude Code per-session scratch: role files are ephemeral, not project state.
.claude/session_roles/
.claude/settings.local.json

# Skill archives are rebuilt from skills/<name>/ by package_skill.py --all.
# A zip of a tracked folder is a cache; git keeps every version of a binary forever.
skills/*.skill

# Harvested Player.log copies: unreproducible, but their value expires once the
# findings are extracted — CLAUDE.md bottom-left quadrant. Keep on disk, never
# in git; a 535 KB log per load is bulk git keeps forever.
observed/**/Player.log*

# resource_watch.sh samples — cache, regenerated by re-running the watcher.
observed/resource_watch/

# validate_patch.py raw sweep output — cache. Reproducible by re-running the
# sweep, and its value expires the moment the findings are extracted; the work
# product is the *_findings.md beside it. 1.7 MB on 2026-08-14.
observed/*_patch_sweep_scoped.txt

# Per-seat liveness stamps written by src/RimMandrake/Utils/say.py. Cache:
# PID-scoped, regenerated on every tool call, meaningless in another session.
infrastructure/state/status/
# derive_matrix.py rebuilds it from the Closes: trailers in git log.
infrastructure/state/closed_ledger.json

# Derived: the 678 MB of contact-sheet PNGs and CSVs regenerate in seconds from
# animal_inventory.py / *_contact_sheet.py. The decisions_*.json do NOT — they are
# the owner's hand-made keep/cut calls and are negated back in below.
# Both paths: the restructure moved this under observed/<stamp>/ and the bare
# rule stopped matching, leaving 21 MB of sheets staged as untracked.
# Contents, not the directory itself: git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded, so the negations below only work with the /* form.
observed/inventory/*
!observed/inventory/decisions_*.json
observed/*/inventory/*
!observed/*/inventory/decisions_*.json

# genome scan outputs are derived: regenerate with genome_scan.py.
# ⚠️ Written as /** with a negation, NOT as `observed/genome/`. Excluding the
# DIRECTORY makes every negation below it unreachable — git never descends into an
# excluded dir — which is how this line silently untracked scan_manifest.json from
# 2026-08-15 until the cleanup audit found it on 2026-08-20. The manifest is the
# only record of which mod set produced the cache, so losing it makes the 340 MB
# of art_cache/ unregenerable rather than derived.
observed/genome/**
!observed/genome/scan_manifest.json

# skill eval run outputs are derived; fixtures and evals.json are kept
skills/skills-workspace/iteration-*/

# modlist_swap.py archives one PRESWAP copy per swap - pure churn, and FULL.LATEST is the one that matters
infrastructure/state/modlists/ModsConfig.PRESWAP.*.xml

# rimflow render output: board.json is rebuilt on a timer and queue_preview/ on every
# render, both from infrastructure/state/ledger/events.jsonl alone. Pure churn in a
# shared worktree. Delete the whole directory and one `render` rebuilds it.
infrastructure/state/derived/

# rimflow's four generated queue views. Rendered from events.jsonl + items/<ID>.md by
# `render.py --overwrite-queues`, exactly like derived/ above. They were tracked AND
# uncommittable until 2026-08-21 — the commit guard refused every regenerated copy,
# because a regenerated view differs from HEAD every time — so git held a frozen
# snapshot while the disk held the truth. HUMAN.md, CHECK_CLOSED.md and
# DECIDE_ARCHIVE.md are HAND-WRITTEN and stay tracked.
infrastructure/state/queue/DECIDE.md
infrastructure/state/queue/BUILD.md
infrastructure/state/queue/CHECK.md
infrastructure/state/queue/REP.md

# Derived ortho globe SVGs — regenerate with worldview.py; the PNGs beside them are committed
world/view/globes_*/*.svg
